---
description: Захватить в хранилище исходной базы изменённые объекты ветки
agent: code
---

Use this command only from an active ready configuration `itldev/*` worktree whose source infobase uses a configuration repository.

Run the helper directly from the current project directory:

If the agent shell tool supports `timeout_ms`, run this lifecycle command with `timeout_ms >= 3900000` by default so the outer shell outlives the 3600-second 1C Designer/Enterprise limit. Do not use `120000 ms` or another short default.

```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\.agents\skills\1c-workflow\scripts\run-itl-command.ps1 -- -Action lock-config-repository-objects
```

The helper maps committed, staged, unstaged, deleted, and untracked configuration delta to official XML object lists and runs only `/ConfigurationRepositoryLock -Objects` against the source infobase. It never loads configuration files or widens the request to the full configuration. New top-level identities need a separate root-only capture (`Configuration includeChildObjects="false"`) before their dependent additions; nested forms and attributes do not. If another repository user owns the root, report that owner, skip only those additions, and request every independent changed object. An unclassified root launch, transport, or timeout failure stops because its mutation result is uncertain. Root ownership never proves individual captures. An empty list is a successful no-op; unresolved or ambiguous identities block before Designer starts. Return a non-empty `userReport` exactly, including for `status=failed`, preserving captures, conflicting owners, root-blocked and not-attempted objects, absent objects, and unconfirmed outcomes. Recover `userReportOmitted` on failure as on success. Preserve failed status and append `requiredAction`; do not replace a partial report with one conflict or automatically retry/unlock. If no report exists and `LOCK_CONFIG_REPOSITORY_OBJECT_CONFLICT` names exact objects and repository users, report it and its `requiredAction` without reading `console.log`. For other failures without a report, read only the last 80 lines of `logPath`.

The shared database queue reserves the source infobase before local lifecycle locks and retains ownership through both requests and confirmed cleanup. Existing owners finish normally; do not close foreign sessions to bypass the wait. Branch and Vanessa service databases are not part of this command's reservation.
